scope: "The FLEET CONSOLE — N Intelligences in one console shell. Realizes [CXC-ICD-D13]. Five parts: (1) the THREE-AXIS identity model (ROLE -> memory + bootstrap tier + agent registration; INSTANCE ID -> topics, telemetry, locks, voice; HOST -> where it renders) and the instancing unit that declares axes 1 and 2; (2) the four data-layer singletons that must be removed (one channel bridge, one telemetry publisher set with a boot-time transcript pin, no roster source, a hardcoded `_app/console/bbox`) plus host-as-a-pane and identity-on-glass; (3) MEMORY SCOPING — the `cwd=None` fork between the two spawn paths, the ROLE-keyed project dir David ratified, ROLE meaning THE WHOLE AGENT ROSTER with derived store names, ONE store at `~/compose-instances/<role>/memory/` reached by two access paths because cwd cannot be the mechanism for a worktree-dispatched subagent, recovery as the SAME role with no surrogate machinery, the re-keying of the existing per-INSTANCE `[CXC-IH-HOMES]` invariant this forces, and the DERIVED memory index without which per-role memory ships a concurrent-write defect; (4) the two-mode (engage/configure) pane and the config-tab splitting rule; (5) the three-tier PLATFORM/ROLE/INSTANCE bootstrap model. The pane itself is AUTHORED as a parameterised composite with zero engine code."
