not-this: "Not a surrogate-access design. An earlier shape in which one role read ANOTHER role's store — with a borrowing rule and a write-attribution invariant — is RETIRED, not deferred: David's reframe removes the problem instead of solving it, because recovery instantiates the ACTUAL role and therefore gets the same memory by the ordinary mechanism ([CXC-FC-RECOVERY-SAME-ROLE]). Not two memory systems: the top-level load and the dispatched-subagent path address ONE store at one location, and reading 'two access paths' as 'two stores' builds the fork the rule exists to prevent ([CXC-FC-STORE-ACCESS]). Not cwd-keyed memory for dispatched roles: a worktree cwd is ephemeral and a prune would destroy the store, which is [INSIGHT-WORKTREE-IS-NOT-THE-ENVIRONMENT] instance (4) applied to memory. Not 'make the console a fleet console' as a rewrite. The composition model is ALREADY plural — parameterised composites, `repeat`, widget-scoped variables and bindable layout order all ship today — so this build removes four singletons from the Python data layer and authors one composite ([CXC-FC-THESIS]). Not a new rasterising widget class for the pane: [SPEC:CXC-PRIM]'s composites-not-code-widgets rule applies in full and a pane widget class is a spec violation, not a shortcut ([CXC-FC-COMPOSITE]). Not per-INSTANCE memory: David ruled PER ROLE 2026-08-12 against the architect's lean, and the reconciliation that follows — key the project dir by ROLE, carry instance identity in INSTANCE_ID and the manifest — is normative and forces a change to an ALREADY-SHIPPED invariant ([CXC-FC-HOMES-REKEY]). Not per-role memory without a derived index: that combination ships the concurrent-write defect and is explicitly refused ([CXC-FC-MEMORY-INDEX-DERIVED]). Not a specification of the Terminal Widget as a backup path — it is an ONGOING keyboard surface, and speccing it as a fallback under-builds it and keeps the console dependent on iTerm ([CXC-FC-BASELINE]). Not a second discovery path, a second slicer or a second transport table ([CXC-FC-ANTI]). Every decision point in this document is CLOSED; nothing here blocks dispatch under [PRINCIPLE-RATIFY-BEFORE-DISPATCH]."
