## 9. Acceptance

### [CXC-FC-ACCEPT-INSTANCING] FC-C1..FC-C3 — the composite and the instancing unit

- definition: two-tier by construction — a machine signal is necessary and, for any surface a human perceives, never sufficient ([PRINCIPLE-MACHINE-GREEN-IS-NOT-GLASS-GREEN]).

| ID | Criterion | when / then | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FC-C1 | Two Intelligences render in one scene from ONE composite | WHEN a scene declares two instances THEN both panes expand with complete, non-colliding bindings | a render test loads a two-pane scene and asserts two disjoint sets of channel/telemetry namespaces, two distinct id roots, and zero duplicate widget ids | **David sees two Intelligences in one console and talks to each.** Mandatory, non-delegable |
| FC-C2 | No rasterising widget class was added for the pane | WHEN the slice lands THEN the pane is a `components:` entry only | a grep guard asserting no new engine Widget subclass is registered for the pane; the pane's definition is a `.compose.yaml` component | — |
| FC-C3 | The instance binding lives at PARAM scope, in one place | WHEN the scene is parsed THEN no document-level `chat_id` variable exists and every channel site derives from the pane's param | `grep -c 'chat_id' intelligence/console/console.compose.yaml` returns 0 for the `variables:` block; a test asserts `start-console-daemons.sh` reads the declared instance list | — |
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLEET]

### [CXC-FC-ACCEPT-MEMORY] FC-C4..FC-C7 — memory scoping, the highest-risk criteria

- warning: FC-C5 is stated in BOTH directions on purpose. "Host and child resolve to distinct memory stores" is TRUE for distinct roles and FALSE for `architect`/`architect-hosted`, which share a role and therefore share a store BY DESIGN under [DD-FC-MEMORY-GRAIN]. A test asserting distinctness for the same-role pair would encode per-INSTANCE memory and contradict the ratified decision.

| ID | Criterion | when / then | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FC-C4 | No spawn path can inherit a cwd | WHEN either spawn path runs for a managed instance THEN cwd is the declared project dir, never None and never the repo | a cross-implementation test drives `IntelligenceHost.spawn` AND the Terminal Widget with the same `(instance_id, role)` and asserts identical resolved cwd; a grep guard that `pty.fork(` is reachable from one cwd-setting site ([CXC-FC-DEFORK]) | — |
| FC-C5 | The project key is keyed by ROLE, and never by the repo | WHEN two DISTINCT roles run THEN `project_dir_key` differs; WHEN one role's host and hosted child run THEN it is the SAME key; in NO case is it the repo's key | three assertions in one test: distinct-role keys differ; same-role keys match; neither equals `project_dir_key(REPO_ROOT)` | David opens `~/.claude/projects/` and sees a dir per role, and no fleet transcript under the repo key |
| FC-C6 | The shipped isolation guard was RE-KEYED, not disabled | WHEN two distinct ROLES claim one home THEN `_enforce_home_isolation` still raises; WHEN one role's two instances share a home THEN it does not | the re-keyed selftest at `host.py:355` onward, asserting both directions and the updated message text naming `~/compose-instances/<role>/` ([CXC-FC-HOMES-REKEY]) | — |
| FC-C7 | The memory index is DERIVED, so concurrent writers cannot corrupt it | WHEN two instances of one role add facts concurrently THEN the regenerated index contains both | a concurrency test asserting both entries survive; an idempotence test asserting two regenerations are byte-identical; a guard asserting no code path hand-edits `MEMORY.md` ([CXC-FC-MEMORY-INDEX-DERIVED]) | David reads the regenerated index and it names every memory file present |
| FC-C18 | EVERY role in the roster has a store, and the store set is DERIVED | WHEN a role descriptor is added THEN that role has a store with no other act | a test asserting the derived store-name set equals the descriptor basenames under `.claude/agents/` plus the FactLattice pool; a lazy-creation test asserting a never-written role has no directory and errors nowhere ([CXC-FC-ROLE-MEMORY]) | David adds an agent def and its first dispatch can write a fact |
| FC-C19 | ONE store, two access paths — a dispatched role's memory SURVIVES a worktree prune | WHEN a dispatched subagent writes a fact from a worktree THEN the top-level Intelligence of that role reads it with no sync step, and a prune destroys nothing | a test asserting the descriptor-stated path and the top-level load resolve to the SAME directory; a prune test asserting the fact survives; a guard asserting no store path resolves under `~/.cache/claude-worktrees/` ([CXC-FC-STORE-ACCESS]) | **David dispatches a role twice and the second dispatch already knows what the first learned.** Mandatory, non-delegable |
| FC-C20 | Recovery is the same role, with no surrogate machinery | WHEN `composeux-architect` is instantiated outside the console under a `recovery-` instance id THEN it resolves the SAME memory store and a DISTINCT channel namespace | a test spawning one role under two hosts with two instance ids, asserting one store and two namespaces; a grep guard that no code path resolves a store for a role other than the caller's own ([CXC-FC-RECOVERY-SAME-ROLE]) | David starts a recovery instance in iTerm and it remembers what the console-hosted one learned |
- note: FC-C18..FC-C20 were added after the narrative's [FC-ROLE-MEMORY] and [FC-RECOVERY-IS-THE-SAME-ROLE] rulings (David, 2026-08-12). They are appended rather than renumbered so an id already quoted elsewhere keeps meaning what it meant.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLEET]

### [CXC-FC-ACCEPT-DATALAYER] FC-C8..FC-C13 — the four singletons, host-as-a-pane, identity

| ID | Criterion | when / then | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FC-C8 | N bridges run and no instance loses its voice | WHEN two instances are declared THEN two bridges hold two distinct flocks and both channels stay live | a test asserting two `composeio-channel-bridge-<id>.lock` files and traffic on both `intelligence/<id>/out` ([CXC-FC-S1-BRIDGES]) | David adds a second Intelligence and his Architect keeps answering |
| FC-C9 | Telemetry is per-instance and the transcript pin is RE-resolvable | WHEN an instance is re-hosted THEN the console re-pins to the new transcript and the stale interval was visible | disjoint `self/<id>/*` namespaces per instance; a re-host test asserting re-pin within a bounded interval and a visible stale marker ([CXC-FC-S2-TELEMETRY]) | David re-hosts an Intelligence and its gauges resume instead of freezing |
| FC-C10 | ONE roster computation, not one per pane | WHEN the console runs THEN exactly one subscriber to `intelligence/+/channel/alive` exists and `fleet/roster` is published once | a grep guard counting wildcard-alive subscriptions == 1; a test asserting an independently-launched peer (never spawned by the console) appears in the roster ([CXC-FC-S3-ROSTER]) | David sees an Intelligence he started himself listed in the console |
| FC-C11 | App geometry no longer collides | WHEN two apps run THEN each publishes to `_app/<app_id>/bbox` | a two-app test asserting two distinct topics; a grep guard that `_app/console/bbox` is not a hardcoded default ([CXC-FC-S4-BBOX]) | placement of a launched window is correct with several apps up |
| FC-C12 | The console has no privileged self | WHEN the host's own pane is instantiated THEN it uses the same composite call as every other | a grep guard that no data source or widget branches on the host id ([CXC-FC-HOST-AS-PANE]) | David cannot tell from the surface which pane is "the console's own" |
| FC-C13 | Identity is on the glass | WHEN any pane renders THEN its instance id and role are visible | a render test asserting both strings present and non-empty in every pane capture | **David looks at a two-pane console and knows which Intelligence he is talking to without clicking.** Mandatory, non-delegable |
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLEET]

### [CXC-FC-ACCEPT-GUARDS] FC-C14..FC-C17 — the surface, and the machine-checkable no-second-path guards

| ID | Criterion | when / then | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FC-C14 | The pane toggles and the tab de-scopes | WHEN a pane is in CONFIGURE THEN its dials bind `intelligence/<id>/config/*` for ITS id, and the console tab holds only console-self plus PLATFORM dials | a test asserting no config-tab widget binds a literal instance id, and that per-pane mode state is independent ([CXC-FC-CONFIG-TAB]) | David configures one Intelligence without touching the other's settings |
| FC-C15 | No second discovery path, slicer or transport table was introduced | WHEN the guards run THEN each of the three has exactly one implementation site | three grep guards, each asserting a count of 1: subscribers to `intelligence/+/channel/alive`; the transcript/session slicing implementation; the bus transport table. A count of 0 FAILS as loudly as a count of 2, so a renamed site cannot pass by disappearing ([CXC-FC-ANTI]) | — |
| FC-C16 | Nothing regresses | WHEN the slice lands THEN every capture for a scene this build did not TOUCH is byte-identical, and no test regresses. The CONSOLE's own capture necessarily changes — the console gaining panes IS the build — and is regenerated ONLY under a glass review | the render capture-diff green for untouched scenes; `pytest intelligence/` plus the render suite green with no unexplained drop in collected count; the expected-drift set is ENUMERATED with a cause per file (nondeterministic vs per-checkout are different defects and must not share a label) | **David reviews the regenerated console capture and accepts it.** Mandatory — a regenerated golden nobody looked at is a golden that certifies whatever it happens to contain |
| FC-C17 | The withheld answer stays withheld, and every gift declares a tier | WHEN a gift file is read whole THEN no answer is returned with it, and every gift resolves to exactly one tier | a guard asserting no `<details>`-withheld answer outside `answers*/`; a test asserting every file under `bootstrap/dusk-gifts/` declares a tier ([CXC-FC-GIFT-MECHANISM], [CXC-FC-GIFT-TIERS]) | a fresh instance reasons a problem through before it can see the answer |
- constraint: FC-C1, FC-C13 and FC-C5's glass leg CANNOT be waived by a green machine run. Every mechanism here can pass in isolation while the console is unusable for a reason only a human at the glass will see — two panes that render identically, a pane labelled with the wrong id, a gauge attached to the other Intelligence.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLEET]

