## 10. Anti-patterns — forbidden BY NAME

### [CXC-FC-ANTI] Five things this build must not do, and why each

- forbidden: TWO CONSOLE INSTANCES -- rejected by [CXC-ICD-D13], and independently by the singletons themselves. Every one of them would fire at once — competing per-`<id>` flocks (there is a `yielding` counter for exactly this), duplicate daemons, N full data layers on one machine. It is forking the app to obtain a variation the composition model already expresses, which [PRINCIPLE-NARROW-WAIST] forbids.
- forbidden: A NEW RASTERISING WIDGET CLASS FOR THE PANE -- [CXC-FC-COMPOSITE]. The composite mechanism is built, tested and already used by eight widgets; a class here duplicates a working mechanism and puts the pane outside the authoring surface every other widget lives in.
- forbidden: A SECOND SLICER, A SECOND DISCOVERY PATH OR A SECOND TRANSPORT TABLE -- reuse by reference. Each is a computation with one right answer, so a second implementation is a guaranteed future disagreement whose symptom appears far from its cause ([INSIGHT-FORK-DIVERGENCE-IS-A-CLASS]). Guarded machine-checkably by FC-C15.
- forbidden: DECIDING TABS-VS-WINDOWS-VS-RAIL UP FRONT -- once the pane is instantiable, presentation is scene authoring, and David has explicitly deferred it. Both can exist from the same widget, so choosing now spends a decision to buy nothing.
- forbidden: SPECIFYING THE TERMINAL WIDGET AS A BACKUP PATH -- [CXC-FC-BASELINE]. A surface specced as a fallback is under-built, and an under-built keyboard path is how the console stays dependent on iTerm.
- forbidden: A SURROGATE OR CROSS-ROLE MEMORY-ACCESS MECHANISM -- [CXC-FC-RECOVERY-SAME-ROLE]. Recovery instantiates the ACTUAL role, so no role ever needs to read another's store; building the mechanism anyway installs an access rule that must be got right forever to solve a problem that no longer exists.
- forbidden: A SECOND MEMORY SYSTEM FOR DISPATCHED ROLES -- [CXC-FC-STORE-ACCESS]. Two access paths reach ONE store; two stores would diverge invisibly, because each caller only ever sees its own.
- see-also: [CXC-FC-COMPOSITE], [CXC-FC-BASELINE], [CXC-FC-RECOVERY-SAME-ROLE], [CXC-FC-STORE-ACCESS]
- reason-note: each prohibition above is enforced by the node named in its value; this property is the traversable form of that list, because a `forbidden:` value is descriptive and mints no edge.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLEET]

### [CXC-FC-OUT] Explicitly out of scope

- out: roster-DRIVEN pane visibility ([DD-FC-PANE-SOURCE] — additive, and deliberately outside acceptance).
- out: the presentation choice — tabs, windows or rail ([CXC-FC-ANTI]).
- out: the Terminal Widget's own contract, which is [SPEC:CXC-TERM]'s and is consumed here unchanged.
- out: any parser or expander change. If the pane cannot be authored with today's `expand_components`, that is a finding to report, not a change to make inside this build ([CXC-FC-COMPOSITE]).
- out: the ordered-container mechanism itself, which is built and tested ([CAP-BINDABLE-ORDER]).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLEET]

