**Version**: 0.1
**Created**: 2026-08-12
**Status**: Draft — every decision point ([DD-FC-MEMORY-GRAIN], [DD-FC-PANE-SOURCE], [DD-FC-PROJECT-DIR-LAYOUT]) is RATIFIED and CLOSED, so nothing here blocks dispatch under [PRINCIPLE-RATIFY-BEFORE-DISPATCH]. Three findings were added by the spec-writer against the narrative and are flagged for the architect's read: [CXC-FC-HOMES-REKEY] (the shipped per-INSTANCE isolation guard REFUSES the ratified per-ROLE layout, so it must be re-keyed rather than bypassed); [CXC-FC-GIFT-MECHANISM] (the `<details>` split already landed in commit 4bca26e, narrowing that requirement to a regression guard); and [CXC-FC-UNIT]'s refinement of the instancing unit from one parameter to the `(instance_id, role)` pair, because `role` is not derivable from `instance_id` and the manifest chain takes it as an argument. Folded in 2026-08-12 after the narrative gained [FC-ROLE-MEMORY] and [FC-RECOVERY-IS-THE-SAME-ROLE]: [CXC-FC-THREE-AXES], [CXC-FC-ROLE-MEMORY], [CXC-FC-STORE-ACCESS], [CXC-FC-RECOVERY-SAME-ROLE], acceptance FC-C18..FC-C20, and two additional named anti-patterns. No surrogate-access design was ever authored here, so nothing had to be retracted — the prohibition is recorded so it cannot be re-derived.
**Intelligence**: composeux-architect / factlattice-editor, 2026-08-12
